WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:28.280
Google revenue growth from $10.6 billion in 2006 to $445.9 billion last year shows the compounding power Canadian investors can capture in their TFSA through long-term tech exposure. This is Modern Investing Techniques, episode 177. Quick reminder, everything we discuss here is for education and entertainment. The practice investment of the day uses simulated trades with no real money.

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:32.560
I'm not a licensed financial advisor and this isn't financial advice.

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:36.320
Always do your own research before putting real money to work.

00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:42.660
The S&amp;P 500 closed at 7,650, up 0.2%.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:52.260
The NASDAQ Composite reached 26,523, up 0.4% for a year-to-date gain of 14.15%.

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:58.820
The TSX composite finished at 35,807 down 0.2%.

00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:04.120
The central bank rate cycle continues to set the macro backdrop for rate-sensitive sectors.

00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:08.780
AI infrastructure remains the dominant leadership theme in equity markets.

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:14.300
Higher bond yields are exerting pressure on growth-oriented names while supporting financials.

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:19.900
The combination creates a clear sector rotation signal that Canadian investors can monitor through

00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:26.400
simple moving average crossovers on sector ETFs. Long-term revenue compounding in technology

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:30.300
names rewards patient holders who avoid chasing short-term rotations.

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:35.920
The Google figures illustrate how a single dominant platform can scale revenue more than

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:42.520
40 times over two decades when network effects and data advantages compound. Canadian investors

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:48.340
can implement this by allocating a fixed percentage of new TFSA contributions each year to a

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:52.320
broad technology ETF rather than attempting to time individual names.

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:57.820
This approach historically outperforms during expansion phases of the business cycle, when

00:01:57.820 --> 00:02:00.960
capital expenditure on digital infrastructure accelerates.

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:06.740
Risks include regulatory pressure and valuation compression if growth slows, so position

00:02:06.740 --> 00:02:10.320
sizing should stay below 10% of total portfolio value.

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:16.680
Pair the allocation with a simple moving average filter on the ETF itself to reduce drawdowns

00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:17.880
during contraction phases.

00:02:18.580 --> 00:02:23.300
The strategy works best when investors commit to annual rebalancing rather than reacting

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:24.480
to quarterly headlines.

00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:29.760
Investors who rebalance once per year capture the majority of the compounding effect,

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:34.420
while avoiding the tax drag that frequent trading can create inside registered accounts.

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:40.440
A second layer of protection comes from tracking the 20-day average volume on the chosen ETF,

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:45.800
and pausing new contributions if volume drops below that benchmark for three consecutive

00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:51.120
of sessions. Historical data from similar platform companies shows that holding through two

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:56.680
full business cycles typically delivers the highest terminal value for patient TFSA holders.

00:02:57.620 --> 00:03:04.020
Imagine you added a technology ETF to your TFSA last month after strong earnings from chipmakers.

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:09.820
Your order filled at the prevailing price yet the ETF later lagged broader indices because

00:03:09.820 --> 00:03:15.480
capital rotated into financials on rising yields. The mechanism at work is relative

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:20.920
performance. Sector's do not move in lockstep because economic indicators such as the yield curve

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:28.020
and PMI readings shift capital between defensive and cyclical groups. Most retail investors assume

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:33.120
their chosen sector will keep leading once it starts outperforming, but the data shows leadership

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:39.560
changes every 6 to 18 months. The pro-tip is to track two simple leading indicators each month.

00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:45.160
The shape of the two-year versus ten-year treasury curve and the latest ISM manufacturing

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:45.740
reading.

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:51.700
When the curve steepens and PMI rises above 50, tilt toward industrials and materials.

00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:55.660
When both flatten, shift toward utilities and consumer staples.

00:03:56.500 --> 00:04:01.120
The concrete misconception to avoid is treating any single sector as a permanent holding

00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:04.200
without checking these cycle signals at least quarterly.

00:04:04.900 --> 00:04:09.460
Investors who ignore the rotation signal often end up holding the previous cycles leaders

00:04:09.460 --> 00:04:12.440
while the new leaders compound at a faster rate.

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:17.720
Checking the two indicators takes less than five minutes once a month and can be automated

00:04:17.720 --> 00:04:21.620
with a simple spreadsheet that pulls the Treasury curve data from public sources.

00:04:22.340 --> 00:04:29.000
The same discipline applies inside an RRSP or FHSA, where contribution room is limited

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:33.640
and every percentage point of outperformance matters over a multi-year horizon.

00:04:34.680 --> 00:04:39.300
This week's simulated weekly hold targets alphabet on the back of its reported annual

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:42.220
revenue of $445.9 billion.

00:04:42.960 --> 00:04:46.820
The position size is $1,000 entered at Monday's open.

00:04:47.560 --> 00:04:52.480
The invalidation level is any session where weekly trading volume falls below the 20-day

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:52.840
average.

00:04:52.840 --> 00:04:58.220
A 5% stop loss caps the maximum loss at $50 on the position.

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:03.980
The target range is plus 3% to plus 7% over the 5 session window.

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:10.160
The medium rating reflects the confirmed revenue catalyst offset by the macro rotation signal

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:11.620
visible in rising yields.

00:05:12.360 --> 00:05:17.460
The pick applies a volume confirmation filter drawn from prior lessons to avoid entering

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:19.640
names already under rotation pressure.

00:05:19.640 --> 00:05:25.740
Listeners see how a single fundamental milestone can anchor a multi-session hold when paired

00:05:25.740 --> 00:05:27.440
with a clear invalidation level.

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:34.340
The 5% stop loss is sized to the $1,000 position so that any breach produces a known dollar

00:05:34.340 --> 00:05:36.580
loss rather than an open-ended drawdown.

00:05:37.240 --> 00:05:41.980
Volume tracking near the 20-day average supports the thesis that the revenue milestone has

00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:43.560
not yet triggered broad selling.

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:46.640
No newly closed trade since the last review.

00:05:46.640 --> 00:05:52.140
The most recent practice investment has already been reviewed, current holdings remain open

00:05:52.140 --> 00:05:57.360
and pending their scheduled evaluation, so there is no new realized result to report today.

00:05:58.020 --> 00:06:03.640
Portfolio performance shows 60 total trades with a 52% win rate across 31 winners,

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:11.000
28 losers and 1 break even. Cumulative profit and loss reaches $299.63.

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:19.640
The matched window alpha versus the NASDAQ composite sits at negative 4.8% across nine rules based trades.

00:06:20.260 --> 00:06:24.020
Average return per trade equals 0.50%.

00:06:24.020 --> 00:06:31.920
The record began on August 18, 2026, under the published rules of five session holds, entered at the next open.

00:06:32.620 --> 00:06:38.500
The negative alpha remains within the early sample range, where statistical significance has not yet been reached.

00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:46.320
Listeners can reproduce every number by applying the same entry, stop, and five session horizon rules to the published picks.

00:06:46.980 --> 00:06:55.560
The 60-trade sample now provides enough data to begin comparing strategy family performance across catalyst event versus earning surprise approaches.

00:06:56.340 --> 00:07:04.820
FinViz allows investors to filter stocks by revenue growth, volume relative to the 20-day average, and sector membership in under two minutes.

00:07:04.820 --> 00:07:14.100
Canadians can export results directly into a TFSA watch list and set alerts for any name crossing above its 200-day moving average.

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:19.860
The free tier covers all required fields for the volume confirmation rule used in today's pick.

00:07:20.460 --> 00:07:29.080
The platform also displays relative volume as a percentage, so users can see at a glance whether today's trading activity exceeds the 20-day benchmark.

00:07:29.920 --> 00:07:38.940
Exporting the filtered list takes one click and preserves the column order for easy import into a spreadsheet that tracks entry and exit dates for the weekly hold.

00:07:39.640 --> 00:07:46.940
Wealth simple trade lets TFSA holders place commission-free equity orders and view real-time volume data on the same screen.

00:07:47.680 --> 00:07:56.540
Users can set a simple alert for any holding when volume drops below the 20-day average, directly supporting the invalidation rule applied to the weekly hold.

00:07:56.540 --> 00:08:02.660
The platform also displays Canadian dollar equivalent prices for US names, removing one

00:08:02.660 --> 00:08:05.320
layer of currency friction for cross-border positions.

00:08:05.860 --> 00:08:11.300
The mobile interface shows the 20-day average volume line overlaid on the price chart, so

00:08:11.300 --> 00:08:14.280
the invalidation level is visible without switching apps.

00:08:14.980 --> 00:08:19.460
Alerts can be configured to trigger once per day, which prevents notification fatigue

00:08:19.460 --> 00:08:22.820
while still catching the first session that violates the volume rule.

